---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Notts Repeaters publishes programming details for GB7NR, GB3NF, and GB3NM."
>
  <p class="kicker">The group</p>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    One site for the three Nottingham repeaters kept by {site.keeper}.
  </p>
  <div class="stack">
    <p>
      GB7NR is the 70cm DMR and D-Star repeater, running Pi-Star. DMR is on SystemX and D-Star is on XLX248 module P. GB3NF is the 2m FM
      repeater, with AllStar links made by the keeper. GB3NM is the standalone
      70cm FM talkthrough.
    </p>
    <p>
      All three are licensed through the {site.region}, RSGB region 13. The ETCC
      record withholds the exact site for GB3NF and GB3NM, so this site publishes
      the locator square and the frequencies you need to programme a radio.
    </p>
    <p>
      Frequencies on the station pages follow the ETCC records checked on 13 October
      2026. When a repeater changes, the station page is the page that changes.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
